===Etymology===
Coined in 1963 for the British science-fiction programme ''[[w:Doctor Who|Doctor Who]]''; said to stand for "Time and Relative Dimension(s) in Space".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɑːdɪs/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɑɹdɪs/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-TARDIS.ogg|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|TARDISes}}

# The [[time machine]] and [[spacecraft]] used by the [[w:Doctor (Doctor Who)|Doctor]] in the British sci-fi television series ''[[w:Doctor Who|Doctor Who]]'', which is larger on the inside than its exterior (that of a [[British]] [[police box]]) suggests, or any of the conceptually similar time machines used by other members of the Doctor's race, the Time Lords.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1986|author=Pip & Jane Baker|title=The Mark of the Rani|chapter=19|page=129|passage='While I was in the Rani's '''TARDIS''', I made an adjustment or two.' He chuckled, remembering the occasion.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2000|author=Fraser A. Sherman|title=Cyborgs, Santa Claus, and Satan|page=57|passage=The Master's essence escapes his funeral urn and lands the '''TARDIS''' in San Francisco on December 30, 1999.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Will Hadcroft|title=The Feeling's Unmutual: Growing up with Asperger Syndrome (Undiagnosed)|page=16|passage=I want the ground to swallow me up. I want to hide in a corner, curl up, and weep, sucking my thumb. I want the '''TARDIS''' to appear and take me away.}}

